8. How the private Kubernetes server connects to GitHub

This is important.

Your Kubernetes master does not need to be publicly exposed.

The connection is:

                 Internet
                    │
                    │ HTTPS outbound
                    ▼
              GitHub Actions
                    ▲
                    │
                    │ persistent connection
                    │
             ┌──────┴──────┐
             │    k8-m1    │
             │             │
             │ Self-hosted │
             │   Runner    │
             └──────┬──────┘
                    │
                    │ kubectl
                    ▼
               Kubernetes

The runner on k8-m1 makes an outbound connection to GitHub.

GitHub does not need to initiate an inbound connection to your private master.

That's why your private Kubernetes network can work with GitHub Actions.

