One important distinction

You currently have CI/CD working, but external Internet access to the HTML page is a separate networking step.

Right now:

GitHub → Runner → Kubernetes → Pods

is working.

The next stage would be:

Internet
   ↓
Public IP / Load Balancer
   ↓
Kubernetes Service
   ↓
HTML Pods

Since your Kubernetes nodes are on a private network, don't expose the Kubernetes API itself to the Internet. For production-style architecture, we'd normally put a public load balancer/reverse proxy in front of the application rather than making the master node public.

This is a good point to stop and save this as your baseline CI/CD lab.
